# Validation with Zod

## Location & naming

All Zod schemas live in `src/lib/validators/{domain}.ts`.

```typescript
// src/lib/validators/beat.ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const createBeatSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  genre: z.string().min(1),
  bpm: z.number().int().min(40).max(300).optional(),
});

export type CreateBeatInput = z.infer<typeof createBeatSchema>;
```

## Rules

- Name schemas as `{action}{Domain}Schema` (e.g., `createBeatSchema`, `beatFilterSchema`).
- Export inferred types as `{Action}{Domain}Input`.
- Parse in API routes before passing to services: `const input = createBeatSchema.parse(body);`.
- Use `z.coerce` for query params that arrive as strings.
- Shared filter schemas (pagination, sorting) can be composed with `.merge()` or `.extend()`.
